cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "estimandYLL: Years of Life Lost via the G-Formula"
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23653505
abstract: >-
  Estimates years of life lost as the difference in restricted expected
  residual lifetime between two binary exposure scenarios on the attained-age
  scale. A pooled logistic parametric g-formula standardizes individual
  conditional survival curves over an explicitly selected baseline population.
  Confidence intervals come from a participant bootstrap or from the empirical
  sandwich variance of stacked estimating equations, which needs a single model
  fit. Includes Poisson and Royston-Parmar model comparators and plotting
  helpers.
authors:
